{"step_index":113,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-18T16:17:40Z","content":"### Why this happens on Desktop Web vs. iPhone:\n\n1. **On a Desktop Web Browser (Chrome/Edge on PC):**\n   - Standard desktop computers do not have mobile rear-facing document cameras. Expo automatically maps `Take Photo` to an **image file upload dialog** so you can upload a photo of a lead sheet from your computer.\n2. **On your Physical iPhone (via Expo Go):**\n   - When running on iOS, `Take Photo` opens the **native iPhone Camera viewfinder** directly, allowing you to physically hold up and snap your paper document.\n\n---\n\n### New Instant Testing Feature:\n\nI have added a **\"Load Sample Lead Sheet (Instant)\"** button to the scanning screen. \n\nIf you refresh your browser tab at `http://localhost:8081`:\n1. Tap **Snap Sheet** $\\rightarrow$ **Load Sample Lead Sheet (Instant)**.\n2. It will immediately parse a realistic 5-lead sheet into the **Interactive Verification Table**.\n3. You can edit names/numbers or click **\"Save List & Launch Power Dialer\"** to jump straight into the live calling HUD!"}
