{"step_index":115,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-18T17:45:27Z","content":"Here are the 2 most reliable ways to connect your iPhone—even with MS Defender active on your phone:\n\n---\n\n### Method 1: The Zero-Friction Expo Account Sync (Recommended)\nThis bypasses all local Wi-Fi, IP routing, and MS Defender VPN subnet restrictions completely by syncing your session through Expo's secure cloud relay:\n\n1. **Create a Free Account** at [expo.dev/signup](https://expo.dev/signup) (takes 30 seconds) if you don't have one.\n2. **Log in on your PC** in your terminal inside `snap-dialer`:\n   ```bash\n   npx expo login\n   ```\n3. **Log in on your iPhone:**\n   - Open the **Expo Go** app on your iPhone.\n   - Tap the profile icon / settings and log in with the **same account**.\n4. **Start the Dev Server on your PC:**\n   ```bash\n   npx expo start\n   ```\n5. **Open on your iPhone:**\n   - In the **Expo Go** app, **SnapDialer** will automatically appear under **\"Recently in development\"** at the top.\n   - Tap it and the app will compile and launch directly on your phone!\n\n---\n\n### Method 2: Direct LAN with MS Defender\nIf you prefer connecting directly over your Wi-Fi router:\n\n1. **Enable Local Network on iOS:**\n   - On your iPhone, open **Settings $\\rightarrow$ Privacy & Security $\\rightarrow$ Local Network**.\n   - Make sure the toggle next to **Expo Go** is **ON** (green).\n2. **MS Defender Check:**\n   - MS Defender VPN on iOS can block local subnet traffic (`192.168.x.x`). Open the MS Defender app on your phone and temporarily pause Web Protection / VPN while testing.\n3. **Start Expo with LAN host:**\n   ```bash\n   npx expo start --host lan\n   ```\n4. In **Expo Go** on your iPhone, tap **\"Enter URL manually\"** and type the `exp://192.168.x.x:8081` address shown in your terminal.\n\n---\n\n### How to Test Live OCR Parsing Once Open:\n\n1. Tap **Snap Sheet $\\rightarrow$ Take Photo of Sheet**.\n2. Aim your iPhone camera at any paper lead sheet, printed roster, or handwritten list and take the picture.\n3. **API Key:**\n   - You can paste a free **Gemini API Key** (from [aistudio.google.com](https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey)) directly into the input field on the screen.\n   - The AI will analyze the photo, extract all names, phone numbers, and company notes, and populate the interactive verification table ready to dial!","thinking":"**Testing Mobile VPN**\n\nOkay, I'm trying to figure out how to test this on the iPhone. The user's only VPN is MS Defender, which might be a problem since it intercepts local subnet traffic. I need to find a workaround to get a clear test result. I'm exploring how the Defender VPN could impact this testing on the iOS device, considering it could be blocking traffic.\n\n\n**Clarifying Connections Methods**\n\nI've got a couple of methods for connecting the iPhone. Direct Wi-Fi with Local Network permission in iOS settings should work if MS Defender isn't isolating the local network. However, there's a foolproof zero-config method using a free Expo Cloud Account. This completely avoids firewall and subnet issues, as both the PC and iPhone connect directly to Expo's cloud relay. I'll test these two approaches to ensure a solid connection.\n\n\n"}
