{"step_index":121,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-18T18:00:43Z","content":"Notice that your phone tried to connect to **`192.168.1.163`**, but you configured **`192.168.1.169`**.\n\nThis happens because Expo Go cached the old IP address, or Windows Defender Firewall on your PC is blocking incoming traffic on port 8081.\n\nHere is the exact 2-step fix:\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Open the Correct URL Manually on iPhone\n\n1. In the **Expo Go** app on your iPhone, tap **\"Enter URL manually\"** (under Projects / Servers).\n2. Type:\n   ```text\n   exp://192.168.1.169:8081\n   ```\n3. Tap **Connect**.\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: If it still times out $\\rightarrow$ Windows Firewall is blocking Port 8081\n\nTo instantly allow Expo through Windows Firewall, open **PowerShell as Administrator** on your PC and run:\n\n```powershell\nNew-NetFirewallRule -DisplayName \"Expo Metro 8081\" -Direction Inbound -LocalPort 8081 -Protocol TCP -Action Allow\n```\n\nThen tap **Connect** again on your iPhone. It will connect immediately and begin bundling the app!","thinking":"**Analyzing IP discrepancy**\n\nOkay, I've hit a potential snag. I've pinpointed an IP address discrepancy. The user's settings indicate 192.168.1.169, however, the phone's error message shows 192.168.1.163. I'm now digging into the root cause of this mismatch.\n\n\n"}
