{"step_index":123,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-18T18:01:07Z","content":"A connection timeout to port 8081 on a Windows PC is caused by **Windows Defender Firewall** blocking incoming connections from your phone.\n\nHere are the 2 fastest ways to unblock it:\n\n---\n\n### Fix 1: Add a 1-Line Firewall Rule (Fastest)\n\n1. Press `Win + X` on your keyboard and choose **Terminal (Admin)**, **PowerShell (Admin)**, or **Command Prompt (Admin)**.\n2. Paste this command and hit **Enter**:\n\n   **In PowerShell (Admin):**\n   ```powershell\n   New-NetFirewallRule -DisplayName \"Expo Metro 8081\" -Direction Inbound -LocalPort 8081 -Protocol TCP -Action Allow\n   ```\n   *(Or in Command Prompt Admin: `netsh advfirewall firewall add rule name=\"Expo Metro 8081\" dir=in action=allow protocol=TCP localport=8081`)*\n\n---\n\n### Fix 2: Set Windows Wi-Fi Profile to \"Private\"\n\n1. On your PC, open **Settings $\\rightarrow$ Network & Internet $\\rightarrow$ Wi-Fi**.\n2. Click your connected Wi-Fi network.\n3. Change **Network profile type** from **Public (Recommended)** to **Private**.\n   *(Windows automatically blocks all device-to-device connections on \"Public\" networks).*\n\n---\n\n### Quick Verification:\nOpen **Safari on your iPhone** and go to `http://192.168.1.169:8081`. \nAs soon as the page loads, open **Expo Go** and tap **Connect**—the app will download and launch on your phone screen!","thinking":"**Diagnosing Connectivity Issues**\n\nOkay, so I've updated my assessment. Turns out that `.163` was a typo, which changes things. The phone was actually hitting `.169:8081` but timing out. This strongly suggests the culprit is Windows Defender when a device on the same Wi-Fi can't connect to the PC on port 8081. This is almost always what causes it!\n\n\n"}
